 "note": "How a buy menu shows what is for sale (UI-020, UI-021; ADR-0044; the owner, 2026-11-24: \"improve all the buy menus (game wide) by showing full 3rd model of object in a grid layout instead of a long list of text with buy btn\", then of look test 33: \"B, and D when narrow\"). Used by the counters of shops, cafes and a mall's outlets and by the building designer's list of pieces (Prototype/play/buymenu.js); checked by world.buy_menu_problems. 'wide' is layout B (a grid of objects, the chosen one large beside it), 'narrow' layout D (small cells, the chosen one described in a strip); a panel narrower than narrow_px shows the narrow one. Sizes in pixels at text size 1. 'goes': the words and the mark for where a bought thing goes (the mark's colour is a board colour of settings.json menu.colours). A thing shows its own object where one is made (a mall good for the home, a piece of furniture); every other thing shows a stand-in: 'stand_in.things' names one for a thing by its id, 'stand_in.wear' by the part of the look a piece of clothing sets (part, shape, the part that gives its colour), 'stand_in.goes' by where it goes. 'shapes': each stand-in as boxes [across, up from the floor, front(-) to back(+), width, height, depth, colour, shade, turned by degrees], metres, the way furniture.js draws; colour is one of 'colours' (linear RGB, ART_DIRECTION 2.3), 'band' (the seller's colour: a mall outlet's sign, else 'bands' by the kind of shop) or 'own' (the colour of the clothing itself). Every number here is a first guess [ASSUMPTION].",
